          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"schema_version\":\"ai-evaluator-v2/1.1\",\"case_id\":\"3-3\",\"candidate_id\":\"candidate_3\",\"action_assessment\":{\"status\":\"preserved\",\"summary\":\"The main business activities are represented: examine claim, write/repeat recommendation, senior review with OK/Not OK outcome, and send back to the claims officer. The main semantic problems arise from routing rather than missing action content.\"},\"flow_assessment\":{\"status\":\"defect\",\"summary\":\"Required precedence is broken: the graph allows completion after writing the recommendation without any senior review, and it places repeated recommendation before the senior check instead of after a Not OK send-back.\"},\"control_flow_assessment\":{\"status\":\"defect\",\"summary\":\"The approval/rework structure is misrepresented. A premature decision is inserted before senior review, the OK path can bypass the mandatory check, and the Not OK path terminates after send-back instead of looping back to repeat the recommendation.\"},\"main_error_type\":\"mixed_or_cascading\",\"explanation\":\"The source requires a mandatory sequence of examine claim -> write settlement recommendation -> senior officer checks and marks OK/Not OK, with Not OK sending the claim back and causing the recommendation to be repeated, and OK allowing the process to proceed. The generated graph instead adds a decision immediately after writing the recommendation, including a direct success path to the end without any senior check. Its retry path performs a repeated recommendation before the senior check, and after a Not OK result it sends the claim back but then ends rather than returning to the recommendation step. Although most action meanings are present, the central approval-and-rework behavior is not preserved.\",\"overall_score\":0.36,\"severity\":\"major\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"ambiguity_flag\":false,\"ambiguity_explanation\":\"\",\"requires_human_review\":false,\"review_reason\":\"\"}"
        }
